  "question": "The business requirements for a service management system are described as follows: The system manages multiple services, each with a service ID, name, type, price and description. There are multiple users in the system, each with a user ID and name. Each service usage needs to record the operating user ID, service ID, usage time and duration. The system needs to support real-time monitoring and performance evaluation of service usage.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0005\nCREATE TABLE `services` (\n  `service_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `service_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `service_type` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`service_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `users` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `service_usage` (\n  `usage_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `service_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `usage_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `duration` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`usage_id`),\n  KEY `service_usage_ibfk_1` (`user_id`),\n  KEY `service_usage_ibfk_2` (`service_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `service_usage_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `service_usage_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`service_id`) REFERENCES `services` (`service_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
